      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are architectural rendering services?",
            "answer": "Architectural rendering services turn architectural drawings (floor plans, elevations, CAD files) into photorealistic images of the finished building. A 3D artist models the structure, applies real materials and accurate lighting, and renders marketing-ready views: interiors, exteriors, streetscapes or aerials. Builders, developers and architects use them to pre-sell, win approvals and market architectural projects before construction is complete."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much do architectural rendering services cost?",
            "answer": "At Bella, photoreal architectural renders start at {price:3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization} per finished image for a residential interior. Commercial interiors, single-building exteriors, streetscapes and multi-building compositions are priced per view in the table above. Every price includes modelling from your plans, revisions and 4K print-ready delivery, and volume discounts of up to 20% apply automatically. Across the wider North American market, expect roughly $300 to $5,000 USD per image depending on complexity."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does an architectural render take?",
            "answer": "Typically one to two weeks from plans to finalized render depending on scope — interiors are usually faster than multi-building exteriors. We confirm timing as soon as you send your drawings."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What do you need to start a rendering project?",
            "answer": "Floor plans or architectural drawings, plus any elevations, material selections and reference images you have. CAD and PDF are ideal, but rough or hand-drawn plans work too — we confirm anything unclear before modelling."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between 3D rendering and architectural visualization?",
            "answer": "They largely overlap: architectural visualization is the broader discipline of communicating unbuilt architecture visually, and 3D rendering is the technique used to produce the final photoreal images. In practice, a studio like Bella provides both — we visualize the project from your plans and deliver the rendered images you market with."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer exterior and landscape rendering services?",
            "answer": "Yes. 3D exterior rendering covers single buildings with landscaping, sky and lighting, and streetscape and aerial site views cover the landscape around a whole row or subdivision. Prices for each view are in the pricing table above."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much do architects charge for renderings?",
            "answer": "Architects either produce renderings in-house as part of their design fees or commission an outside rendering studio. Studio prices across North America run roughly $300 to $5,000 USD per image depending on complexity and realism. Bella works directly with architects, builders and developers, from {price:3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization} per image."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is an architectural rendering called?",
            "answer": "Architectural renderings are also called architectural visualizations, 3D renders, CGI or archviz. Before construction they are often called pre-construction or construction renderings. All describe the same thing: a photorealistic image of a building created from its plans."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a rendering company?",
            "answer": "A rendering company, or architectural visualization studio, is a team of 3D artists that turns plans into photorealistic images for marketing, approvals and client presentations. Bella is a rendering company working with home builders, developers and architects across the US and Canada, with clients including Concord Pacific, Highland Homes and Rockwood Legacy Residences."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can ChatGPT do architectural renderings?",
            "answer": "ChatGPT and other AI image tools can generate a picture of a building, but they don't build from your dimensioned plans, so proportions, windows and rooflines often drift from the real design. They are useful for early design ideas and mood boards. For images buyers, lenders or planning boards rely on, a 3D artist working from your drawings is still the standard."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What software is used for architectural rendering?",
            "answer": "Studios commonly model in 3ds Max, SketchUp or Revit, render with a dedicated rendering engine, and finish the image in post production in Photoshop. You do not need any of it to order: send your drawings and our 3D team does the modelling."
          }
        },
        "q12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I order interiors and exteriors together?",
            "answer": "Yes, and for a development it is the normal case. Add each render type to the same order; the building is modelled once, and volume discounts apply across the whole set."
          }
        },
        "q13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the benefits of architectural rendering?",
            "answer": "A render communicates design intent to people who do not read technical drawings. Clients and planning boards see materials, light and scale before anything is built, so design issues surface on screen instead of on site, approvals and sign-offs move faster, and builders and developers can market and pre-sell a project before construction begins."
          }
        },
